From 36119dc057b2b755e36820aa95da6d4fe8d37698 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Longwei Yang <19267252+Longwei-Yang@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:40:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 12/17] Safarium: make everyday features work, hide the ones
 that can't

Bubbles: Chrome anchors its password, address, bookmark and translate
bubbles to its own location bar; Safarium registers its address field as
that anchor (safarium_bubble_anchors) and gives the window an autofill
bubble handler, so saving passwords and addresses, autofill, Bookmark This
Tab and the QR code work. Address bubbles find the handler through the tab
(Safarium windows have no BrowserView); the eyedropper and emoji panel are
wired to the window.

Context menu: Reading Mode and Listen open in the side panel (the immersive
view needs Chrome's page area); the Lens overlay is off (it CHECKs without
that page area), so image search opens Google in a new tab and "Ask Google
about this page" is gone.

Removed what can't work here: Cast (needs Chrome's toolbar), Google
Translate settings (needs Google API keys), "AI in Chrome" settings, the
sync / Google services row, and View > Always Show Toolbar in Full Screen
(Safarium's toolbar doesn't read it).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
